Paved access road at 401 Alder Street.  Key locked fence gate for water tank compound and key locked door into base of water tank where radio equipment is located.  Sprint facility is straight ahead on left side of access road next to utility tower.  

Access requires COI and access agreement on file with OCWA.

For NTP and construction scheduling, must schedule construction with landlord through Megan Thomas, Esq. (mthomas@ocwa.org /315-455-7061 Ext. 3129) and Terry Mathewson (mathewson@ocwa.org / 315-455-7061).  A secondary LL contact is Andrew J. Weiss P.E. BCEE, OCWA, Executive Engineer/Chief Engineer, ajweiss@ocwa.org, 315-455-7061;  

For access, all Contractors, on behalf of T-Mobile, are required by LL to contact OCWA in advance and schedule their arrival and complete OCWA's Access Agreement process before entry will be granted.  Access requires that Contractor provide its COIs and have a signed Access Agreement on file with landlord OCWA.  Contacts for COIs and access agreement are also Megan Thomas, Esq. (mthomas@ocwa.org /315-455-7061 Ext. 3129) and Terry Mathewson (mathewson@ocwa.org / 315-455-7061).  A secondary LL contact is:  Andrew J. Weiss P.E. BCEE, OCWA, Executive Engineer/Chief Engineer, ajweiss@ocwa.org, 315-455-7061;  

Primary Access Contact is Terry Mathewson at mathewson@ocwa.org by e-mail and/or phone at 315-455-7061.  LL OCWA requires climbing certificates and verification of up-to-date insurance prior to accessing/climbing the tank.  48-hour notice is requested by LL for routine work.  You must arrange access escort in advance with OCWA. Vendor to reimburse LL for security while on site. 

Terry Mathewson (info above) is primary access contact.  Alternate access contact if cannot reach Terry Mathewson - Operations Department Matt Chabot, (W) 315-455-7061 X 3116, (M) 315-399-8751, chabot@ocwa.org.

